  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Pterobunocephalus is a genus of small to medium-sized aspredinid species. Members of this genus are distinguished from all other aspredinids by the following characters:</p><ul><li>an extremely depressed (flattened) head and body</li><li>head ornamentation highly reduced or absent</li><li>often a distinct notch in the upper jaw</li><li>10–20 anal fin rays</li></ul><p>Females of this genus carry embryos directly attached to the ventral surface of their bodies, which also distinguishes them from all other aspredinids.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>South America: Amazon River basin of Brazil and Peru. Type locality: Trombetas-river, near Obidos, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Small species that can probably be kept as per other members of this family with a quiet tank with sand and plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Tablet foods and small live foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: The genus name Pterobunocephalus: pterus, referring to large anal fin of Bunocephalus (subgenus Pterobunocephalus) albifasciatus (= P. depressus). The specific name dolichurus: dolichos, long; oura, tail, referring to its \"very long\" tail relative to others then classified in the short-tailed subfamily Bunocephalinae.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Despite the little information available on this species and the few occurrences, this species has a wide range and no major threats, and is therefore assessed as Least Concern (IUCN 2021).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/aspredinidae/pterobunocephalus_dolichurus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Ferraris, C.J. Jr., 2007. Checklist of catfishes, recent and fossil (Osteichthyes: Siluriformes), and catalogue of siluriform primary types. Zootaxa 1418:1-628. Frederico, R.G. 2021. Pterobunocephalus dolichurus. The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species 2021. Friel, John Patrick (1994-12-13) (PDF). A Phylogenetic Study of the Neotropical Banjo Catfishes (Teleostei: Siluriformes: Aspredinidae).</p>"
    }
